// RevMFA schema TEMPLATE. Two equivalent ways to adopt — pick ONE:
//
//   (A) A dedicated UserMfa model (shown below), one row per user, related
//       back to the host's own user/person table. This is the default the
//       Prisma reference adapter (`createPrismaMfaStore`) expects.
//
//   (B) Inline the same columns onto an existing user model instead of a
//       separate table (see the commented block at the bottom). Then wire a
//       thin custom MfaStore rather than the reference adapter.
//
// RevMFA never imports a generated client — the Prisma reference adapter is
// structurally typed and only needs these column names.
//
// Notes for the host:
//   * `userId` is the OPAQUE key RevMFA is keyed by. Wire it to your own user
//     table (StaffUser, Person, User…). RevMFA never interprets it.
//   * `secret` holds the TOTP secret. If you pass a `secretEncryptionKey` to
//     `createAuthMfa`, RevMFA stores the AES-256-GCM ciphertext here; without a
//     key it stores the raw base32 secret (STRONGLY prefer supplying a key — a
//     leaked DB then does not hand an attacker every user's live TOTP seed).
//   * `enabled` is false between `beginEnrollment` and a successful
//     `confirmEnrollment`; `verify()` only succeeds once it is true.
//   * `backupCodeHashes` stores SHA-256 hex digests of the one-time recovery
//     codes — never the codes themselves. Modeled here as a scalar String[]
//     (Postgres native array). On a DB without array columns, store a
//     JSON-encoded string and decode in your store adapter.
//   * `enrolledAt` is stamped at successful confirmation.

model UserMfa {
  id     String @id @default(cuid())
  userId String @unique
  // user   StaffUser @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  // TOTP secret — AES-256-GCM ciphertext when a secretEncryptionKey is set on
  // createAuthMfa (recommended), otherwise the raw base32 secret. Null before
  // enrollment begins and after disable().
  secret String?

  // False until confirmEnrollment succeeds. verify()/verifyBackupCode() are
  // no-ops (return false) while this is false.
  enabled Boolean @default(false)

  // SHA-256 hex digests of single-use backup codes. Consuming a code removes
  // its digest from this list. Empty until enrollment is confirmed.
  backupCodeHashes String[]

  enrolledAt DateTime?

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([userId])
}

